FAITHFUL-PARITY NOTE (states)
  The web TimeMarker is a pure presentational annotation (props → <ReferenceLine>, with the single
  conditional `if (x == null || x === '') return null`). Its data source useAlertContext is
  useSearchParams() + useMemo — a SYNCHRONOUS URL read with NO fetch, NO Promise, NO React-Query.
  Neither has a loading / error / stale / offline branch (there is nothing to load, fail, go stale,
  or lose connectivity to). Per the Honesty Covenant (#2 no scope narrowing, #5 no parity shortcuts,
  and "no stubs/invented chrome"), fabricating such states would contradict the source. This surface
  therefore reproduces the source's REAL branches — context-absent (hasContext=false → no marker),
  timestamp-absent/unparseable (x==null/'' → no marker), marker-present, and the four severity
  variants incl. the legacy warning/error/fatal/ok aliases — exactly as the accepted sibling
  anonymous chart primitive ChartTimeRangeContext (0069) did and passed.

